  "prediction": "The report reveals that in the period from 2016 to 2017, Customs and Border Protection (CBP) identified approximately 308,000 packages for further inspection out of a total of 434 million international mail and express consignments. Of these, around 278,000 packages were inspected, and about 29,000 were cleared without inspection. The primary reasons for selecting packages for further inspection were country of origin, sender information, and recipient information. The report also highlights the challenges faced by CBP in collecting and using Advance Electronic Data (AED) from international postal and express carriers to target mail for inspection. The report recommends that CBP and the United States Postal Service (USPS) should evaluate the costs and benefits of collecting AED for targeting mail for inspection compared to other methods. The report also suggests that CBP and USPS should articulate performance goals for pilots using AED and assess their success in enabling USPS to provide targeted mail to CBP for inspection. The Department of Homeland Security concurred with these recommendations.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report reveals that in the period from 2016 to 2017, Customs and Border Protection (CBP) identified approximately 308,000 packages for further inspection out of a total of 434 million international mail and express consignments. Of these, around 278,000 packages were inspected, and about 29,000 were cleared without inspection. The primary reasons for selecting packages for further inspection were country of origin, sender information, and recipient information. The report also highlights the challenges faced by CBP in collecting and using Advance Electronic Data (AED) from international postal and express carriers to target mail for inspection. The report recommends that CBP and the United States Postal Service (USPS) should evaluate the costs and benefits of collecting AED for targeting mail for inspection compared to other methods. The report also suggests that CBP and USPS should articulate performance goals for pilots using AED and assess their success in enabling USPS to provide targeted mail to CBP for inspection. The Department of Homeland Security concurred with these recommendations.",
